ault":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-07-27T19:27:50Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T10:29:28Z","closed_at":"2026-08-18T12:10:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121833","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121833.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121833.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-18T12:10:34Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/84777\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15279\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nGDScript does allow string literals as multiline comments to some extends. E.g. they are excepted in a top level context, in contrast to other literals.\r\n\r\n> Note: This PR does not break compat. Using string literals at the top level is still accepted. What this PR does, is making string literals subject to \"standalone expression\" warnings.\r\n\r\nThis was introduced for 4.x with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72971. I think it made sense at the time, since it was in 3.x.\r\n\r\nHowever it did surprise me that this was an (supposedly) intended thing, because:\r\n- the sentiment I've gathered during my time on the project from multiple people, was that this is a python thing and we should use comments in GDScript (see e.g. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112523#issuecomment-3506629541, https://forum.godotengine.org/t/how-to-write-multiline-comments/33257, https://forum.godotengine.org/t/commenting-code/58366, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/21310#issuecomment-415325729)\r\n- It is not mentioned at all in the [comment section of the GDScript reference](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#comments).\r\n- The [literal section of the reference](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#literals) also makes no mention of it.\r\n- I have it on safe authorithy that this does not exist /s  \r\n\r\n<img width=\"682\" height=\"153\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9dae25a-a089-4cbd-afcd-a31b62f7f891\" />\r\n\r\nAll of this might be case for documentation. __tl;dr__ However as outlined in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112523 the comment stripping that is offered by binary tokenization does not apply to string literals, so encouraging users to do this is a footgun. As such I think we should phase out this feature during 4.x.\r\n\r\nIn a scope context there is simply no good way to tell apart a user error and a \"multi-line comment\". And I'd rather warn users than keep an undocumented feature.\r\n\r\n> [!Note]\r\n> I don't know how controversial this is. So if necessary I can open a proposal about it.\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121833/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121833/timeline","performed_via_github